div.p:
—He had led Labor Party for 13 years, 8 of them as Prime Minister, longer than
                    any peacetime predecessor this century, and served on the Front Bench nearly 30
                    years;

—Wilson’s closest confidants, in addition
                    to Queen, have been aware for several months of his intention to resign near his
                    sixtieth birthday;

—Best explanation for resignation is the simplest, i.e., Wilson’s own publicly announced reasons; recent
                    left-wing revolt, if it had any effect, merely delayed announcement a few
                    days;

—While Conservative leader Thatcher has already called for general election,
                    government will resist and we believe prospects for early election are remote;
                    moreover, assumptions about outcome of general
